  "about": [
    "Fixture prefixes of apps/server/test suites (R0-00-WT-ISOLATION). Enforced by apps/server/src/core/config/fixture-prefix-registry.spec.ts.",
    "A new prefix is a 4-character head plus '_': k<NN><a-z>_ for an R0 packet, v<NN><a-z>_ for a V1 packet, NN = the packet number (R0-12 -> k12a_). The packet that adds the suite adds {prefix, owner, packet} here.",
    "A new suite cleans up with LIKE ${sqlLikePrefix(P)} from test/helpers/sql-like.js, in its own file and in every helper it imports from apps/server/test, and embeds its prefix in every literal written to User.email, Business.slug, Payment.providerPaymentId, PaymentLink.token or Site.subdomain.",
    "A prefix is found as `const P = '...'`, as `const <UPPER_NAME> = '<x>_'`, or as a '<x>_' string passed as a call's first argument (buildBoundaryFixture('kab_')). Every *.integration.test.ts must own a registered prefix or be listed in noPrefixSuites with a reason.",
    "legacy: true marks the prefixes in use before R0-00 landed (c2f6f46d, plus 'ab_' from R0-05). They keep their names; the set may shrink but never grow. A packet branched before R0-00 that adds a suite renames its prefix to k<NN><a-z>_ and switches its cleanup to sqlLikePrefix() when it is integrated."
  ],
